{
  "$schema": "../theme.schema.json",
  "name": "Metalwork Factory",
  "description": "Welders, furnace keepers and a crane driver, a works gate, and a soot, steel and ember colour scheme under sodium lamps.",
  "company": "Cinderhill Ironworks",
  "branch": "Furnace Lane Works",
  "titles": {
    "manager": "Works Manager",
    "receptionist": "Timekeeper",
    "cleaner": "Floor Sweeper",
    "temp": "Apprentice",
    "vendor": "Pie Trolley",
    "itSupport": "Works Electrician"
  },
  "manager": {
    "name": "Gwen Hartshorne",
    "look": {
      "head": "boss",
      "skin": "warm",
      "build": "normal",
      "outfit": "looseTie",
      "hair": "#3b2a20",
      "eye": "#3a2a1e",
      "shirt": "#e8e2d4",
      "outer": "#2f3542",
      "tie": "#c4561e",
      "collar": "#e8e2d4",
      "pants": "#3a332c",
      "shoes": "#1e1a18"
    },
    "lines": [
      "Whistle goes at eight sharp. I'll be up on the gantry with a mug.",
      "I can see the whole floor from up here. Yes, Declan, including that.",
      "Overtime is approved. Gratitude is approved. Pies are pending.",
      "We don't rush a pour. We plan it, we check it, then we pour it.",
      "Safety first, tea second, and everything else after the tea.",
      "Proudest shop floor in the county. Don't tell them I said so."
    ]
  },
  "receptionist": {
    "name": "Doreen Ashworth",
    "look": {
      "head": "receptionist",
      "skin": "rosy",
      "build": "small",
      "outfit": "buttonCardigan",
      "hair": "#9a9086",
      "hairHighlight": "#b8b0a6",
      "shirt": "#efe8d8",
      "outer": "#2e5a4a",
      "collar": "#efe8d8",
      "pants": "#3a3f4a",
      "shoes": "#2a2220",
      "glasses": "#6b2a22"
    },
    "lines": [
      "Cinderhill gatehouse. Clock in first, then tell me your troubles.",
      "Hard hat, goggles, boots. Visitors get a lanyard and a lecture.",
      "Your card went in upside down again. The clock has made a note.",
      "Deliveries go round the back. Follow the smell of hot iron.",
      "I've signed in three lorries, a pigeon and the forklift. Busy morning."
    ]
  },
